    "text": "An elementary T I-subgroup V of a finite group G is said to be a subgroup\nof non-root type if 1 ̸= NV (V g ) ̸= V for some g ∈ G. Describe the finite groups G\nwhich contain a 2-subgroup V of non-root type such that [V, V g ] = 1 implies that all\ninvolutions in V V g are conjugate to elements of V .                  A. A. Makhnëv",
